{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1534974-thoughts-on-gladiatorial-games","id":1534974,"title":"Thoughts on Gladiatorial Games","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-30T18:56:44-07:00","id":1534974,"title":"Thoughts on Gladiatorial Games","content":"I was perusing the Strix Chronicles this afternoon and re-read the entry on the Strix <b>The Ringmaster</b>. It starts with the usual banter about Rome's Gladiators, &quot;the superstars of their era&quot;, glory to the winner, death to the loser.<br /> <br /> The thing is, that's not true.<br /> <br /> Gladiators could become quite famous, sure, but the real stars were the Chariot Racers. And the Gladiators didn't fight to the death, in fact some had long careers with wins and losses. Execution by animals in the arena was for criminals, it was a distinct event entirely.<br /> <br /> Of course, being historically accurate is besides the point for the setting, much less for the introduction of a Strix. But thing is, I actually think accuracy here would add to the game. Please, bear with me.<br /> <br /> As much as it is a fun trope, the 'all fights are to the death' rule runs its course fast. You can only keep stakes that constantly high so long, maybe lose a lot of characters, and can't keep the games around without stretching disbelief. As a rule of thumb, you have the games for a single story, or even chapter, and that's it.<br /> <br /> My take is that toning down such fights so death is at least uncommon improves the usability of such games to the story. You can actually have a long chronicle or stable setting with an arena as either fixture or focus, tempt the PCs to try their luck, and still have a lethal match from time to time.<br /> <br /> For the Ringmaster it is doubly so, as it is one of the best Strix to have as a long term presence in the game, everything about it makes it a complex character with numerous uses, but the fact the death matches make for a transitory element.<br /> <br /> Now, am I the only one to think like that? What are your thoughts on the matter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-01T07:52:00-07:00","id":1535006,"title":"","content":"I think historical accuracy is kind of a tough sell because who the most popular events were, and things like how frequent deaths were (deaths happened at the hippodromes too, NASCAR didn't invent people going to the races just to see the crashes), varied significantly over the course of history. Just from the Republic to the end of the Western Empire, we're talking roughly a thousand years. Public events waxed and waned in popularity and content.<br /> <br /> That said, I do agree that the Ringmaster could benefit from a change in the direction you're thinking. I think there is a problem where the Ringmaster has to escalate over what's already available. Big name professional wrestling (which is scripted and still risky enough that people have died in the ring), and things like UFC are readily available international entertainment. How popular small promotion wrestling (still scripted) is, is more local, but legal in many places and amps up the danger (even if far more show than not, it's still riskier) to help draw in crowds. Etc.<br /> <br /> If the Ringmaster is offering something on par with callous small promotion wrestling risk taking, we're still in real-world events, so the Strix isn't really adding much there.<br /> <br /> I think a good middle ground is making use (if a bit homebrewed) of the Strix existing familiarity with animating the dead. A stable of animated corpse jobbers that the Ringmaster can pull from at any time to say, &quot;See, it's just smoke and mirrors, we don't really do death matches, it's for show&quot; while actually doing death matches would extend their presence in the narrative a lot by adding a layer of manipulation and deception to what's really going on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-01T11:38:15-07:00","id":1535031,"title":"","content":"Most of the Ringmaster writeup could be just a callous Daeva anyway, and his powers don't even support what he's supposed to be good at doing.<br /> <br /> What he does as a Strix, and that is his appeal to me, is to prey upon people's Humanity indirectly. He has people either participating on or appreciate a show that is a Breaking Point. He creates a context that makes debasing yourself seems enjoyable and innocuous.<br /> <br /> Even without death, a fight between supernatural combatants for the enjoyment of the Kindred would easily be violent enough to afford a Humanity 4 Breaking Point. And with <i>some</i> &quot;safety&quot; it would attract even more direct participants and spectators.<br /> <br /> That would make a long run plan more effective, with the occasional accident or actual death battle taking care of the last vestiges of Humanity.<br /> <br /> On top of that, he could have death battles using Draugr or Revenants, or other undesirables meant for destruction in the Domain. That way he's slowly creating the very stock he'll later use to debase even more Kindred, and he may be secretly promoting conditions for the rise of Revenants.<br /> <br /> Anyway, he's more an example than anything of how the trope of the &quot;Gladiatorial Games&quot; can be more useful for the story if made less immediately lethal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-01T12:25:21-07:00","id":1535033,"title":"","content":"The most recent book I've read on the subject of ancient Rome, &quot;Emperors of Rome&quot;, published recently and authored by an acclaimed academic on the subject, says both that gladitatorial careers did actually tend to be short and brutish, and that being a gladiator offered little prestige.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-01T13:18:25-07:00","id":1535035,"title":"","content":"Short and brutish isn't the same as 'fighting to the death' by a mile, and can still be said of most fight sports nowadays. It is part and parcel of hurting people for sport that people risk being more hurt than they expect.<br /> <br /> And that's my point, how much the difference between death as a risk and death as a certainty affects the game.<br /> <br /> For actual historical accuracy, which was more of an inspiration than actual intent, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> said it all: it is far more complicated, because a lot of factors changed throughout the long history of the Roman Circus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-02T10:11:12-07:00","id":1535081,"title":"","content":"Actually, my apologies, I had misremembered some of the details. Mary Beard does in fact point out that, between the evidence and thinking through the logistics, deliberate fights to the death must have been fairly uncommon, it's just that she couches that in emphasizing the point that the whole sport did still entail horrific violence (and no small amount of social stigma) for those involved in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-07T20:23:27-07:00","id":1535246,"title":"","content":"The Roman-games was responsible for lions and other animals in Northern Africa going extinct. <br /> <br /> Lupine games?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-08T17:00:34-07:00","id":1535310,"title":"","content":"While not to discount the ecological impact of using animals as sport, the Romans didn't invent killing animals for entertainment, nor did they drive any animal into extinction on their own. The Roman games sapped the populations of certain animals in North Africa such that the local populations didn't survive continued trophy hunting that lasted into the 20th century, but that's not the same thing as driving something extinct. Atlas bears and Barbary lions are local subspecies to the brown bear and sub-Saharan lions, who of which existed in the wild until the 1900s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}